WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.230
A container ship docks.

2
00:00:02.280 --> 00:00:05.110
Cranes swing steel boxes onto the quay.

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:11.790
In 2024, the world's container ports handled
about 913 million twenty-foot equivalent

4
00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:12.890
units.

5
00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.470
Right beside many ports
stand heavy industries:

6
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.830
steel mills and oil refineries.

7
00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:21.250
Why build a giant factory
at the water's edge,

8
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.150
when its raw materials come from far away?

9
00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:27.150
In this mission, you'll
weigh resources, labor,

10
00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:31.670
markets and transport, to find
the cheapest place to build.

11
00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:36.710
Then you'll see how the shipping container
lets factories sit far from their customers.

12
00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: explain why so many
big factories sit right beside ports,

13
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.590
even when their raw
materials come from far away.
